                        "username": "branupama"
                    },
                    "message": "why do we need NOT operation, instead we can directly check for if(l_ptrToErrType) is true and do the required return?\n\nsame for below API as well."
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/src/event_logger.cpp",
                    "line": 386,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "What difference it will bring to the existing code?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/src/event_logger.cpp",
                    "line": 386,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jinu Joy Thomas",
                        "email": "jinu.joy.thomas@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jinuthomas"
                    },
                    "message": "agree this will not impact anything. IMO it seems correct"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/src/event_logger.cpp",
                    "line": 386,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Souvik Roy",
                        "email": "souvikroyofficial10@gmail.com",
                        "username": "souvik1914581"
                    },
                    "message": "From code readability point of view, I think using ternary operator instead of `if else` would be better.\n\n`return l_ptrToErrType ? *l_ptrToErrType : types::ErrorType::InternalFailure;`\n\nThis reduces LOC as well."
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/src/event_logger.cpp",
                    "line": 386,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "> From code readability point of view, I think using ternary operator instead of if else would be better.\n\nThat's a personal opinion. \nAnd then comes the question to what level it is more readable than if/else?"
                },
                {
